    },
    "body": "A newly reached fragment fails at a prefix where the selected parent already failed conditionally. This adds an offline generic first-divergence capture endpoint and preserves the matched saved-score diagnosis. Serving operators are unchanged.\n\nOne missing target-free native frame and independent saved arithmetic show unchanged BASE donor, bridge, raw Generate and continuation scores. Prefix updates narrow the direct Copy gap but do not restore the desired fragment; all matched full pools still choose the rival. The candidate remains unselected. Existing feature distinction supports a prospective joint ordered-fragment learning question, without establishing feasibility or useful language capability.\n\nThe capture, Rust report seals, immutable runtime, independent arithmetic and expert result reviews are privately preserved and freshly SHA-verified. Final-head scoped validation is being completed and will be posted before protected queue admission. No gradient, fit, autoregressive repeat or full 512 evaluation ran in this diagnostic.\n\nReferences #820.",
